=======================================================================
 FluxTorrent
=======================================================================

 A modern, self-hosted web front-end for qBittorrent, Transmission and
 Deluge, with built-in torrent search powered by Prowlarr.

 FluxTorrent is a maintained fork of the long-dormant TorrentFlux /
 TorrentFlux-NG project (https://github.com/epsylon3/torrentflux),
 brought up to date for a modern stack: PHP 8, remote-daemon torrent
 backends, Prowlarr search, Docker packaging and a refreshed dark UI.

 The Markdown edition of this file (README.md) is the primary, rendered
 version on GitHub -- see it for the full, formatted documentation.

 NOTE: FluxTorrent is for managing your own legal downloads on a server
 you control. You are responsible for how you use it.

-----------------------------------------------------------------------
 What's modern about it
-----------------------------------------------------------------------

 * Runs on PHP 8.1+ (tested on PHP 8.5). All removed-API usage
   (ereg/split, magic quotes, PHP-4 constructors, curly string
   offsets, preg /e, each()) has been fixed.

 * Database layer uses the maintained ADOdb via Composer
   (mysql -> mysqli, sqlite -> sqlite3 automatically).

 * Choice of torrent backend, selectable in the admin UI:
     - qBittorrent  (Web API, v4 and v5)
     - Transmission (RPC)
     - Deluge       (Web JSON-RPC)
   Add, start/stop, delete (with or without data), rate-limit, seed-
   ratio limits and per-file priorities all work through the client's
   own API -- no CLI clients are spawned by the web server. Torrents
   added directly in the daemon, or via magnet, are adopted into the
   transfer list automatically. Configure under Admin > Transfer
   Settings.

 * Torrent search is powered by Prowlarr (the old scraper engines for
   long-dead sites were removed), with a live indexer dropdown that
   syncs from Prowlarr. Configure the Prowlarr URL and API key under
   Admin > Search Settings.

 * Always-visible top navigation and a built-in dark theme that follows
   the OS preference by default.

 * In-browser HTML5 media player with seeking (HTTP range).

 * Dead bundled libraries (Swift Mailer, reCAPTCHA v1, vlib mail) were
   removed; the torrent maker now uses mktorrent.

-----------------------------------------------------------------------
 Quick start (Docker)
-----------------------------------------------------------------------

     git clone https://github.com/JawshTheDark/torrentflux-ng.git fluxtorrent
     cd fluxtorrent
     docker compose up -d
     open http://localhost:8000/setup.php

 Then:

   1. Complete first-run setup (SQLite DB, download path /downloads/).
   2. Log in -- the first login creates the superadmin account.
   3. Admin > Transfer Settings: pick your Active Backend and fill in
      its connection details.
   4. Admin > Search Settings: set the Prowlarr URL and API key.
   5. Add indexers in Prowlarr and you're ready to search and download.

 See the notes at the top of docker-compose.yml for the bundled
 qBittorrent + Prowlarr wiring.

